  @doc """
  Checks if two strings are almost equivalent.

  Two strings are almost equivalent if:
  1. They have exactly the same set of characters.
  2. For every character, the absolute difference in its frequency between the two strings is at most 3.

  The function handles empty strings (two empty strings are almost equivalent).
  Time complexity is linear in the length of the strings.
  """
  @spec almost_equivalent?(String.t(), String.t()) :: boolean()
  def almost_equivalent?(str1, str2) do
    freq1 = count_chars(str1)
    freq2 = count_chars(str2)

    same_set?(freq1, freq2) and same_frequency_diff?(freq1, freq2)
  end

  @doc """
  Counts the frequency of each character in a string.
